From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:48:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 197/342] usb_webcam: the UVC add-on, built and working (M45)

The UVC code had been left out of the build since 2010. Built again,
with what kept it from working on the C920:
- the frame index requested is the descriptor's own (1-based) one, not
  its place in the list (320x240 asked for 320x180);
- commit sends the camera's probe answer, and a short probe answer
  fails;
- the alternate setting is chosen by bytes per microframe (packet size
  times high bandwidth transactions), not by the raw wMaxPacketSize;
- the endpoint searches used the wrong loop variable;
- YUY2 is converted to B_RGB32 (BT.601), where a Bayer demosaic from the
  Sonix code was;
- the deframer resets its buffer for each frame, ends a frame at an FID
  toggle or EOF, drops frames with ERR, of the wrong size, or partial
  (the first), and keeps only the newest frame waiting;
- its own data pump keeps four transfers of 32 microframes queued
  (BUSBEndpoint::QueueIsochronous()), so the stream has no gaps;
- StopTransfer() lets the pump finish before the alternate setting goes
  back to 0;
- the producer runs at 30 frames a second (5 left a 30 fps camera's
  frames waiting).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
